+## 8. GRPO-refined binder model (SC arm)
+
+`leflur-binder-3di-grpo-sc` is the `leflur-binder-3di` checkpoint after **GRPO**
+reinforcement learning. Rollouts were generated with the `generate_binder_3di_best`
+sampler and scored by a combined reward:
+
+- **interface 3Di-distribution distance** — steer the interface 3Di-state
+  composition toward a Proteina-Complexa reference distribution,
+- **backbone clash** — penalize binder–antigen interpenetration (the dominant
+  reward-hacking mode of the pure-distribution arm),
+- **3DZD interface shape-complementarity (SC)** — reward geometric complementarity
+  of the interface patch (the `w_shape=1` term this arm is named for).
+
+The step-125 snapshot de-clashes and tightens the interface: offline it pulls the
+interface contact fraction toward the native distribution and the effect transfers
+to fully held-out antigens (weaker, as expected for an RL-refined policy). It is a
+**research checkpoint** — a refinement of the published `leflur-binder-3di`
+baseline, not a new state-of-the-art pass-rate claim — and is **internal-only**
+(not yet mirrored to HuggingFace), so its config points at the materialized
+Lightning snapshot on the shared filesystem and defaults to `paths=internal`.
+
+Run it against your own target (side-chain packing is baked in):
+
+```bash
+uv run python -m lobster.cmdline.generate \
+    --config-name experiment/generate_binder_3di_grpo_sc \
+    generation.input_structures=/abs/path/to/my_antigen.pdb \
+    generation.target_chain=B \
+    generation.epitope_indices="[10,12,44,45,47]" \
+    generation.binder_length="[70,120]" \
+    generation.n_designs_per_structure=50 \
+    output_dir=./out/my_target_grpo_sc
+```
+
+Each design writes the usual backbone `*_complex.pdb` **plus** an all-atom
+`*_complex_packed.pdb` (see §9). To run the full Complexa benchmark with this
+model, pass the config through the portable runner:
+
+```bash
+uv run python examples/run_complexa_binder.py \
+    --config experiment/generate_binder_3di_grpo_sc \
+    --n-designs 100 --out-dir ./out/complexa_grpo_sc
+```
+
+Once the checkpoint is uploaded to HuggingFace, switch `model.ckpt_path` to the
+registry short name `leflur-binder-3di-grpo-sc` and run with `paths=public`.
+
+## 9. Side-chain packing — all-atom outputs
+
+LeFlur emits **backbone-only** structures: `writepdb` writes N/CA/C plus an
+idealized O and Cβ, but no rotamers. For downstream tools that need full atoms
+(interface analysis, Rosetta scoring, visualization), enable the optional
+post-generation **side-chain packing** step. It re-reads each generated PDB,
+rebuilds every side chain **in process** with the LigandMPNN side-chain packer
+(fixed sequence = the design's own sequence), and writes an all-atom
+`<name>_packed.pdb` next to it. Multi-chain complexes are packed **together** so
+interface side chains inform each other's χ torsions.
+
+This works with **any** generation mode (binder, monomer, forward/inverse
+folding). It is **off by default** and **on** in
+`experiment/generate_binder_3di_grpo_sc`. Turn it on for any run:
+
+```bash
+uv run lobster_generate \
+    --config-name experiment/generate_binder_3di paths=public \
+    generation.input_structures=/path/to/target.pdb \
+    generation.target_chain=A generation.epitope_indices="[155]" \
+    generation.pack_side_chains=true \
+    generation.packing.glob='*_complex.pdb' \
+    output_dir=./out/binder_packed
+```
+
+Or, for an unconditional monomer run:
+
+```bash
+uv run lobster_generate --config-name experiment/generate_unconditional \
+    paths=public generation.num_samples=10 \
+    generation.pack_side_chains=true \
+    output_dir=./out/uncond_packed
+```
+
+Packing knobs live under `generation.packing`:
+
+| Knob | Default | Meaning |
+|---|---|---|
+| `device` | `cpu` | Packer device. CPU-viable (~0.66 s/design @ 8 threads); scale by fanning out CPU workers rather than contending for the GPU queue. |
+| `num_denoising_steps` | `3` | LigandMPNN packer denoising steps. |
+| `num_samples` | `4` | Rotamer samples drawn per residue (best kept). |
+| `glob` | `*.pdb` | Which PDBs to pack. **For binder runs set `*_complex.pdb`** — otherwise the `*_binder` / `*_target` / `*_initial_structure` split files are each packed separately. `*_packed` / `*_esmfold` files are always skipped. |
+| `ligandmpnn_path` | `null` | Override the LigandMPNN install dir (else `$LIGANDMPNN_PATH` or the default `/cv/home/lisanzas/LigandMPNN`). |
+| `sc_ckpt` | `null` | Override the packer checkpoint (else `$LIGANDMPNN_SC_CKPT` or `ligandmpnn_sc_v_32_002_16.pt`). |
+
+**Requirements.** Packing needs a LigandMPNN install on disk (`$LIGANDMPNN_PATH`)
+and its side-chain packer checkpoint. It is intentionally not a hard LeFlur
+dependency; a run with packing enabled but LigandMPNN missing logs a warning per
+structure and leaves the backbone PDBs untouched (the run itself never fails).
+
